This terminal has a synthetic Metasploit harness loaded. Run:

  msfconsole "RHOST=... RPORT=... TARGETURI=... PAYLOAD=..."

You'll need four values:

  RHOST       — from stage 1
  RPORT       — from stage 1
  TARGETURI   — from stage 2 (the captured request that didn't 403)
  PAYLOAD     — read modules/ to find the right exploit, then
                pick from its COMPATIBLE PAYLOADS list. Check
                payloads/ to confirm architecture compatibility.

The harness will tell you why if it fails. Read its output.

Tip: the right module matches stage 2's CVE AND it's the *exploit*,
not the detector. There are two hits for the CVE.
